From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u, winewayland: add a lightweight focus debug channel.

+win is too heavy for timing-sensitive focus bugs and makes them go away.
The focus channel only logs foreground and active window changes, where
each one came from (application call, SetWindowPos, mouse click,
cross-thread activation, host state change), and in the Wayland driver
how keyboard enter/leave events are turned into foreground changes.

Use with PROTON_LOG=+focus (or WINEDEBUG=+focus).

Refs: https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/877
---
--- a/dlls/win32u/defwnd.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/defwnd.c
@@ -29,6 +29,7 @@
 #include "wine/server.h"
 
 WINE_DEFAULT_DEBUG_CHANNEL(win);
+WINE_DECLARE_DEBUG_CHANNEL(focus);
 
 #define WINE_MOUSE_HANDLE       ((HANDLE)1)
 #define WINE_KEYBOARD_HANDLE    ((HANDLE)2)
@@ -2247,6 +2248,7 @@
                 top = parent;
             }
 
+            TRACE_(focus)( "caption click activates %p\n", top );
             if (set_foreground_window( top, TRUE, FALSE ) || (get_active_window() == top))
                 send_message( hwnd, WM_SYSCOMMAND, SC_MOVE + HTCAPTION, lparam );
             break;
